* Glue for sim/manual. No device model in this file was written for the project:
*
*   LM393.sub   the long-circulated LM393 macromodel (header: "created using PARTS version 4.03 on
*               03/07/90"), included unchanged. Its origin could not be confirmed; the copy is
*               from github.com/semianalog/mod12003. It has a PNP input pair, so an input above
*               the supply simply turns its transistor off, as note 8 of the onsemi data sheet
*               describes.
*   AO3400A_L1  the SPICE level-1 MOSFET with six numbers taken or derived from the typical
*               values of the AOS data sheet rev 3.1: threshold 1.05 V; KP, RD and RS from RDS(on)
*               19 mohm at 4.5 V and 24 mohm at 2.5 V; gate-source 580 pF (Ciss - Crss) and
*               gate-drain 50 pF (Crss at 15 V), as overlap capacitances of the default 100 um
*               wide device.
.include "LM393.sub"

* the two comparators of one package, pins in the order of the SOIC-8
.subckt LM393_PACKAGE outa inan inap vee inbp inbn outb vcc
XA inap inan vcc vee outa LM393
XB inbp inbn vcc vee outb LM393
.ends

* three-pin wrapper: the bulk is tied to the source, as in the part
.subckt AO3400A_L1 d g s
M1 d g s s AO3400A_M1
.model AO3400A_M1 NMOS(level=1 VTO=1.05 KP=80 RD=9.4m RS=6m CGSO=5.8u CGDO=0.5u)
.ends
